+    // kimi-k3-spark patch 0074: LLAMA_PREFILL_SLICE_SAME_FREE=<tokens> (default 0 = off): a prompt with at most that
+    // many tokens left is not held to LLAMA_PREFILL_SLICE_SHARE_SAME, it is read at once as without the pieces. The
+    // same-class share exists so that answers do not stop while a long prompt is read; for a prompt of a few tokens
+    // there is nothing to protect (the answers wait for one or two short ubatches, as they always did), and holding
+    // it back costs time: the clients that already generate run in smaller batches until it has joined them (three
+    // to five short prompts arriving together: 1.2 to 2.6 % of a 256-token round on the GH200 in window nc6, 1.3 to
+    // 3 % on the Spark in window nc-s2). The share against a higher class (LLAMA_PREFILL_SLICE_SHARE) is not
+    // touched, and the prompt's time still counts in the accounts.
+    static int64_t pp_same_free() {
+        static const int64_t v = std::max(0, env_int("LLAMA_PREFILL_SLICE_SAME_FREE", 0));
+        return v;
+    }
+
     // does slot a's prompt go before slot b's (same class)? With patch 0072 a prompt whose rest fits in one ubatch
     // first (fewest tokens left first). Then a prompt that has not started yet, then the one whose last ubatch is
